# T-3466 — R5b daily telemetry rollup (T-2250 GO)
# Source of truth: /opt/termlink/.context/cron/telemetry-rollup.crontab (git-tracked)
# Installed to:    /etc/cron.d/termlink-telemetry-rollup (USER field syntax — do NOT load into a user crontab)
#
# Once a day, after UTC midnight (02:30 host time = 00:30Z in summer, 01:30Z in winter): roll up
# yesterday's local telemetry (queue flaps, reconnects, breaker trips, hub-outage samples, dead
# letters) into one aggregate and post it to telemetry:daily (retention days:400) through the
# durable offline queue. Raw data stays on the host. Not a canary: the .log holds one success line
# per day; diagnostics go to .stderr (T-2685).
#
# --catch-up 7 (T-3615): a host down at 02:30 used to lose that day for good (.107 missed
# 2026-10-24: it was off from 10-25 01:10 to 11:40). Now each run also rolls up any day of the
# last week this host never posted, after its first posted day, flagged "catch_up": true.
# Reading the topic before the run lands (00:30Z in summer, 01:30Z in winter) shows yesterday as
# MISSING; that is not a miss (the 10-27 "miss" was read at 00:10Z on 10-28).
SHELL=/bin/bash
TERMLINK_WORKER_CLASS=background
PATH=/root/.cargo/bin:/usr/local/bin:/usr/bin:/bin
30 2 * * * root cd /opt/termlink && bash scripts/telemetry-rollup.sh --catch-up 7 >> .context/working/.telemetry-rollup.log 2>> .context/working/.telemetry-rollup.log.stderr
